<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      The wallet's foreground service (BIT-126).

      Declared here rather than in :app because it is this module's component:
      :app names a WalletService implementation in one Hilt module and nothing
      else, and an app that had to also remember a <service> line would be an app
      where forgetting it produces a node that starts and is frozen minutes later
      with no error anywhere.

      The two permissions it needs are declared in :app's manifest instead, with
      the rationale next to the others. That split is this repo's convention and
      the reason for it is in that file: a permission is a claim on the Play
      listing and in the system dialog, so it is a decision that should be
      visible in the app's own manifest rather than arriving through a merge.

      android:exported="false" — nothing outside this app may start the wallet.
      It is the AGP default for a service with no intent filter; stated because
      "the default is safe" is not something a reader can check.

      android:foregroundServiceType="dataSync" — required from API 34, and it
      must match the type passed to ServiceCompat.startForeground or the call
      throws. See WalletForegroundService's class comment for why dataSync and
      what its API 35 time cap costs.
    -->
    <application>
        <service
            android:name=".host.WalletForegroundService"
            android:exported="false"
            android:foregroundServiceType="dataSync" />
    </application>

</manifest>
